 the polite request: “Could you ____ the garden fence, please?”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"measure"},{"id":"B","text":"measures"},{"id":"C","text":"measuring"},{"id":"D","text":"to measure"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"Could makes the request less direct, but the following verb still uses its **base form**.","explanation":"After modal **could**, use base **measure**. The question functions as a request.","keywords":["polite-modal-request"],"skill":"polite-modal-request","contextKey":"imperatives-3","fingerprint":"1f30108f182ac0a16700eaa5fe8398973cae9485235de2335cc3de062c5a3220","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-verbs-reference"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Could makes the request less direct, but the following verb still uses its **base form**.","After modal **could**, use base **measure**. The question functions as a request.","Choose **measure**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"After modal **could**, use base **measure**. The question functions as a request.","B":"A modal is not followed by a third-person -s form.","C":"Could requires the base verb here, not an -ing form.","D":"There is no to after could in this request."}}},{"id":"0a94743b-bc62-57fb-aae2-f85d92663e58","topicSlug":"imperatives","level":"A1","prompt":"Give a direct instruction: “____ the travel leaflet, please.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"To translate"},{"id":"B","text":"Translate"},{"id":"C","text":"Translates"},{"id":"D","text":"Translated"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Use a **base verb** for the instruction.","explanation":"An imperative starts with the base verb **translate**; the subject you is understood.","keywords":["positive-command"],"skill":"positive-command","contextKey":"imperatives-4","fingerprint":"579d6a59018ca859ec492f1d457fd5f4a1006a1f238f2163e195d8384c150b02","source":"seed","